Third-party upstream crates
================================================================================
This product depends on, and gratefully acknowledges, the following upstream
open-source crates (each under its own license; see their repositories):

  - c2pa (c2pa-rs), Adobe Content Authenticity Initiative — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  - rcgen — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (generates the seal's self-signed X.509 signing certificate for C2PA)
  - sigstore-rekor, sigstore-tsa, sigstore-merkle, sigstore-crypto,
    sigstore-types (the sigstore-rust workspace) — Apache-2.0
    (sigstore-tsa requests + verifies the RFC 3161 TSA timestamp token;
    sigstore-rekor submits the Rekor v2 DSSE entry; sigstore-merkle does the
    RFC 6962 inclusion recompute; sigstore-crypto verifies the Ed25519 C2SP
    checkpoint signature against the pinned shard key)
  - reqwest — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (HTTPS client for the Rekor v2 shard health check + submit)
  - base64 — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (Rekor entry body / verifier key <-> anchor JSON encoding)
  - tokio — MIT
    (private current-thread runtime driving the sync TSA + Rekor network calls)
  - rustls-pki-types — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (CertificateDer for the best-effort TSA certificate-chain check)
  - ed25519-dalek — BSD-3-Clause
  - RustCrypto: hmac, sha2 — MIT / Apache-2.0
  - RustCrypto: scrypt, chacha20poly1305 — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (passphrase-encrypted keystore at rest, native-only: scrypt is the memory-hard
    KDF (RFC 7914) deriving the key from the passphrase; chacha20poly1305 provides
    the XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD whose decrypt returns an Err on a wrong passphrase)
  - rusqlite (with the `bundled` feature) — MIT
    (local receipt index DB, native-only: a convenience/discovery layer recording
    where receipts live; `bundled` compiles SQLite from source so no system
    libsqlite3 is required. The index is rebuildable from receipts, never a
    source of truth)
  - glob — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (expands `seal` glob patterns, e.g. `out/*.png`, when the shell did not)
  - rmcp (official Model Context Protocol Rust SDK) — MIT
  - clap — MIT / Apache-2.0
  - serde, serde_json — MIT / Apache-2.0
  - mime_guess — MIT
  - wasm-bindgen, js-sys, web-sys — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (the in-browser verifier crate `sealchain-wasm` and c2pa-rs's wasm32 layer)
  - serde-wasm-bindgen — MIT
    (maps the per-layer verify result into a JS object for the web verifier)
  - console_error_panic_hook — MIT / Apache-2.0
    (routes a wasm panic to a readable browser console error)
